WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.115 --> 00:00:01.856
- Hey, do you wanna go down to the beach

00:00:01.856 --> 00:00:03.516
and we'll both roller skate

00:00:03.516 --> 00:00:04.596
with a rope in between us

00:00:04.596 --> 00:00:06.570
until we get so much centrifugal force

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.369
that we fly into billboards?

00:00:08.369 --> 00:00:10.493
- Yeah, but can I do,
like, a sweet grind, first?

00:00:10.493 --> 00:00:11.887
- Of course you can!

00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:14.957
But if any humans come, run.

00:00:16.728 --> 00:00:18.829
Gushers commercials,
where all the kids' heads

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:20.245
turned into fruit.
- Turned into fruit

00:00:20.245 --> 00:00:21.127
and they exploded.

00:00:21.127 --> 00:00:22.114
No one was concerned!

00:00:22.114 --> 00:00:23.171
- Nobody died.
- No one was concerned.

00:00:23.171 --> 00:00:24.506
- Nobody died.

00:00:25.796 --> 00:00:26.849
- [Voiceover] Making funny faces was

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:28.648
such a big deal back then.

00:00:28.648 --> 00:00:29.507
(sucking noises)

00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:30.413
Hate the man?

00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:31.515
Make funny faces.

00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:33.048
The man hates funny faces.

00:00:33.048 --> 00:00:34.429
- This Pop Tart spinning through

00:00:34.429 --> 00:00:36.612
the vacuum of space is incredible.

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:38.365
- What is this part where a plane

00:00:38.365 --> 00:00:39.932
flies around an apple?

00:00:39.932 --> 00:00:41.627
- It's part of a well-balanced breakfast.

00:00:41.627 --> 00:00:42.474
- What are you talking about?

00:00:42.474 --> 00:00:44.215
I never eat airplanes for breakfast.

00:00:44.215 --> 00:00:46.015
- This is the girl from The O.C. as a kid.

00:00:46.015 --> 00:00:47.385
- That's not Misha Barton, no way.

00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:50.862
- That's totally Misha Barton!
(laughing)

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:54.013
- Plain daylight, no one's at the beach?

00:00:54.013 --> 00:00:55.790
Hard to believe, Capri Sun.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:56.905
- See, it's like Alex Mack!

00:00:56.905 --> 00:00:58.274
- Boom, straight into the billboard.

00:00:58.274 --> 00:01:00.167
Walking through a fence
- That was pretty cool.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:02.773
- Was like the coolest
thing you could ever do.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.192
- Oh my God!

00:01:06.192 --> 00:01:08.270
- No (silly noises)

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:09.616
- He is a demon!

00:01:09.616 --> 00:01:10.766
- Parents were so nervous that kids

00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:12.890
were just having sex and doing drugs,

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:13.865
but these kids were just like,

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:15.235
I'm hungry for cereal!

00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:16.453
- Kids dressed so cool back then.

00:01:16.453 --> 00:01:17.870
They always had, like, a bike helmet on

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:18.811
for no reason.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.772
- This kid is dressed like
the Fresh Prince of Bel Air.

00:01:20.772 --> 00:01:22.014
- I still think he's cute.

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:23.025
I kind of love him.

00:01:23.025 --> 00:01:25.892
- He's not not cute, but
he's also terrifying.

00:01:25.892 --> 00:01:27.587
- I love how they always
add, like, the toast

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.212
with the one thing of butter.

00:01:29.212 --> 00:01:30.547
And milk and orange juice.

00:01:30.547 --> 00:01:32.759
Come on, Mom!

00:01:34.053 --> 00:01:36.293
- Raccoon looking for food in the winter.

00:01:36.293 --> 00:01:37.629
- Wait, is that?

00:01:37.629 --> 00:01:38.891
- No, no!

00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:40.655
- It's gonna be a snowboard, you idiot!

00:01:40.655 --> 00:01:41.990
(laughing)

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:42.976
- Oh my God.

00:01:42.976 --> 00:01:44.150
- Oh my God!

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.728
- Bam. Animal cruelty.

00:01:45.728 --> 00:01:47.794
- What's that movie, with
Arnold Schwarzenegger,

00:01:47.794 --> 00:01:49.385
when his eyes burst out of his head?

00:01:49.385 --> 00:01:50.515
- Twins.

00:01:50.515 --> 00:01:51.515
- No.

00:01:51.515 --> 00:01:53.245
- [Man] Stupid idea.
[Woman] His outfit is amazing!

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:55.462
- Aw, man, that's what
rad dudes looked like.

00:01:55.462 --> 00:01:58.858
- I wanna be a rad dude.

00:01:59.781 --> 00:02:02.544
- When I think about why
I loved the '90s so much,

00:02:02.544 --> 00:02:04.424
I just think about watching TV.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.781
- I think these commercials
promoted the fact

00:02:06.781 --> 00:02:08.464
that it's super cool to be a kid.

00:02:08.464 --> 00:02:10.426
- I definitely got enough
of a nostalgia dose

00:02:10.426 --> 00:02:11.946
just watching these.

00:02:11.946 --> 00:02:13.561
- Kids like goofy bull
(beep) and I know it.

00:02:13.561 --> 00:02:14.326
And it's cool.

00:02:14.326 --> 00:02:16.625
Goofy bull (beep) is great.

00:02:16.625 --> 00:02:20.386
(funky music)

00:02:20.386 --> 00:02:21.641
- I'm big in goofy bull (shit),

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.196
but I just don't buy it as much anymore.

00:02:23.196 --> 00:02:24.057
I make it now.

